# K03 NS-ROLES-VIS (the author, 2026-10-07; semantics #declaration-visibility): the root's source reading of
# `b: h` takes h for a Structure value only if h's typed reference names a Structure visible there; Later is defined
# below it, so the type position is unknown where it stands -- refused at the type, not taken as a binding above.
# (The written `@: T h value` form is used only to place T below its type position; it is not reread here.)
@: Later h Later
b: h
Later:
    int: v 4
end: Later
fn: m () int
    return: 7
end: m
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
